.TH "bup\-demux" "1" "2026\-09\-01" "Bup 0.34" ""
.SH NAME
bup\-demux \- demultiplexes data and error streams from standard input
.SH SYNOPSIS
bup demux
.SH DESCRIPTION
Note: this is an internal command, and may be removed or changed at any
time.
.PP
\f[CR]bup demux\f[R] reads standard input as a bup \[lq]multiplexed\[rq]
stream of data from standard output and standard error, and reproduces
that output on its own standard output and standard error.
It\[cq]s primary purpose is to support \f[CR]bup\-on\f[R](1).
.SH SEE ALSO
\f[CR]bup\-on\f[R](1), \f[CR]bup\-mux\f[R](1)
